# Findings Trivy reports that are deliberate, each with the reason. Keep this
# short: every entry is a check that no longer runs.

# DS-0002: "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile".
# The container starts as root on purpose, and only for as long as it takes the
# entrypoint to adopt the owner of the bind-mounted ./data folder; it then drops
# to that user with su-exec before the app starts. A fixed USER line would break
# every host whose user id is not the one hard-coded (see docker/entrypoint.sh).
# CI's "Confirm the app is not running as root" step verifies the drop happens.
DS-0002
